  "body": "See https://github.com/w3c/largest-contentful-paint/issues/111#issuecomment-1370885556\r\n\r\nIMG `decode()` returns a promise that resolves when an image is fully decoded. Doesn't that leak information about cross-origin no-cors images? e.g. an SVG for a logged-in vs. anonymous user have the same dimensions but the logged-in one is a lot more complex so takes a long time to decode.",
